Subject: Software rasterizer: no shared counters in the pixel loop, cheaper texel addressing

Every raster worker incremented the same statistics for each pixel, so one cache line bounced
between cores (the main menu drew at 16 frames/s). Counts are kept per worker and added once per
triangle. The guest memory base is read once, power-of-two wrap is a mask and the DXT cache slot
uses a shift.

---
diff --git a/src/kernel/nv2a_pb_exec.c b/src/kernel/nv2a_pb_exec.c
--- a/src/kernel/nv2a_pb_exec.c
+++ b/src/kernel/nv2a_pb_exec.c
@@ -833,6 +833,8 @@
     int32_t sc = (int32_t)c, n = (int32_t)size;
     if (!size)
